MotionVFX graphics and effects can be dropped into a video timeline, and 3D titles and graphics can be added to a scene on moving surfaces or at a natural depth that matches camera movement. Masking improvements make it quicker to add outlines, accents, motion trails, and more to video subjects, and static photos and illustrations can be turned into animations.<br/>
<br/>
There's a new Content Hub with access to stock video, photos, graphics, and backgrounds. Creators can also generate images in FCP with text descriptions, and then edit those images. Any image from an FCP project can be opened in Pixelmator Pro for editing, and then added back to FCP when editing is finished.<br/>
<br/>
Apple added easing options for more precise control over animation, and there's a new timeline command for detaching a clip from the primary storyline to reposition it freely without affecting B-roll, titles, and audio.<br/>
<br/>
The new features are included in the Creator Studio version of Final Cut Pro, so you will need a Creator Studio subscription to use them. Creator Studio is priced at &#36;12.99 per month and includes access to Final Cut Pro, Logic Pro, Pixelmator Pro, Motion, Compressor, and special features in free apps like Pages, Keynote, and Numbers.<br/>
<br/>
The one-time purchase version of Final Cut Pro does not include the new additions.<br/>
